  "text": "Recipe: Millet Crackers\nCreator: Padma Subramanian\nCategory: Cracker\nIngredients: 1 cup rolled oats, 1/2 cup any millet flour (I used jowar flour), 1/4 cup white sesame seeds, 1/4 cup sunflower or pumpkin seeds, 1/4 cup black sesame seeds, onion powder, garlic powder, 'dhaniya' (coriander) powder, 'jeera' (cumin) powder, 'lal mirch' (red chillies) powder, Chaat Masala, 'aamchur' (dry mango powder), salt (to taste), 1 1/4 cup water (we can use upto 1/4 cup more)\nCooking methods: bake\nInstructions: Add 1 1/4 cup water (we can use upto 1/4 cup more) so that it's lumpy pouring consistency. Pour on a baking sheet in very thin even layer. Bake at 350F for 10 mins. Cut into squares. Bake again for 40 mins or till crispy.\nNotes: Inspired by \"Be a Plant Based Woman Warrior\" (2022) by Jane & Ann Esselstyn. For Indian theme, I added Indian spices.",
